  "description": "On the streets of Beijing, you'll find spicy lamb skewers coated in cumin and chile flakes. But there's no need to go to China to have them—you can make them on the grill.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: vegetable oil → canola oil\n\nNotes: For the most flavorful, tender, and juicy skewers, don't trim off any of the fat from the shoulder chops. Pre-soaking the bamboo skewers for at least two hours or even overnight before using is an important step to prevent them from burning during grilling.",
